      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Is the Super Scoop practically capable of transportation on water, counsel?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (David B. Kaplan)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what -- what I'm saying is historically there has never been a decision in which a dredge was not considered a vessel until this case that we appear here now."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Was -- was it a vessel?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Lisa S. Blatt (United States, amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BLATT: Thank you, Justice Stevens, and may it please the Court: Justice Ginsburg, I take it the reason that the scow was not relied on is because the petitioner worked 99.9 percent of his time on the Super Scoop and petitioner never made the argument that he had a connection to the scow."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do you think we need to use the word practical or practically in section 3?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Frederick E. Connelly, Jr. (respondent)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If there are no questions, we would ask that the First Circuit's decision be reversed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, I think in that -- in that -- using your hypothetical, it's a construction platform right off the coast. They'd send everyone home. If there was any trouble with the sea, the -- the greatest perils that are discussed in the petitioner's brief -- and they list them all -- one of them is isolation and far away from home and far from aid. Those don't apply to Mr. Stewart. Mr. Stewart would be sent home if there was too much -- the weather got bad. He would be sent home in a -- in a minute or 2. He lived right in Boston. He was in"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Super Scoop was inspected regularly by the State, Federal, and Government officials and by the general contractor on the job."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But how do you -- how can you possibly describe as a bright line test anything that says you have to identify the primary function?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hillsman",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0003-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In his amicus brief filed on behalf of the petitioner, Mr. Hillsman writes that the lower court unanimously -- unanimously -- have decided that the definition of vessel for purposes of the Longshore Act is much, much more inclusive than it is for the Jones Act, and it has worked perfectly fine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The term vessel can and often has had a different meaning for the Jones Act, which this Court has stated is a vessel in navigation, than it does with the Longshore and Harbor Workers Act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professor Schoenbaum",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Professor Schoenbaum has said that the mutual exclusivity of the two acts is really in theory only and that there are always cases and will be dealing with the brown water seamen and brown water employees, harbor workers and longshoremen, where they're going to have to be covered under both anyway."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-814",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "505b0a69c5017893a4c91f366f475a5311a8fff0e9b9cfcf525828415436af7b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-505b0a69c501-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    }
  ],
